    English and in UK English"), throughout the Phonology bullets, and the
    entire IPA column of the New Testament Greek phonology table are empty, so
    the sound changes are described but never given a value. I dropped the
    pronunciation sentence that consisted only of empty brackets, reworded the
    Phonology bullets so they do not point at absent symbols, and reproduced
    the table as it stands. The two sample texts appear in the source as one
